76","guid":"928e518a-111f-36b0-a486-1a15c453f91f","fullName":"Peden Stadium","address":{"city":"Athens","state":"OH","zipCode":"45701","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/3876.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":12237},"article":{"headline":"Nick Poulos accounts for 3 TDs, including go-ahead score, to help Ohio edge Ball State 35-28","description":"— Nick Poulos accounted for three touchdowns, including the go-ahead score with 1:16 remaining, as Ohio rallied in the fourth quarter to beat Ball State 35-28 on Tuesday night.","story":"ATHENS, Ohio -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5228762/nick-poulos\" target=\"_new\">Nick Poulos</a> accounted for three touchdowns, including the go-ahead score with 1:16 remaining, as Ohio rallied in the fourth quarter to beat Ball State 35-28 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              The Bobcats (8-3, 6-1 Mid-American Conference) trailed 20-14 entering the fourth before <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5155789/darren-james-hamilton\" target=\"_new\">Darren James-Hamilton</a> returned a <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5075392/keldric-luster\" target=\"_new\">Keldric Luster</a> interception 34 yards for a touchdown. Poulos then scored on a 12-yard run to give Ohio a 28-20 lead.\n\n\r\n              Ball State (3-8, 2-5) answered with TJ Horton’s 2-yard touchdown run and a two-point conversion to tie it at 28 with 2:23 left.\n\n\r\n              Ohio responded with a six-play, 66-yard drive, and Poulos found <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5193110/dom-dorwart\" target=\"_new\">Dom Dorwart</a> for a 29-yard touchdown with 1:16 remaining.\n\n\r\n              Ball State reached the Ohio 49 on its final possession, but Luster was sacked before James-Hamilton broke up a fourth-down pass with 5 seconds left to seal the win.\n\n\r\n              Luster threw for 257 yards and two touchdowns and rushed for 109 yards. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5191056/donovan-hamilton\" target=\"_new\">Donovan Hamilton</a> caught a 10-yard touchdown in the second quarter, and after <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4709774/quentavius-scandrett\" target=\"_new\">Quentavius Scandrett</a> intercepted Poulos, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5162689/eli-hohlt\" target=\"_new\">Eli Hohlt</a> scored on an 80-yard reception to help Ball State build its halftime lead.\n\n\r\n              Poulos threw for 155 yards and rushed for 58 yards and two scores. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5228764/riley-neer\" target=\"_new\">Riley Neer</a> had five catches for 92 yards for Ohio.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Ball State: Plays Central Michigan at home on Nov. 28.\n\n\r\n              Ohio: Hosts Toledo in a regular-season finale on Nov. 27.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-18T15:13:26Z"}}